Core Processing Logic

This module contains the main automation engine responsible for reading, populating, and validating PDF forms.

⚙️ Key Features
Batch Processing
Automatically detects and processes all PDF files passed into the system
Dynamic Input Handling
No hardcoded filenames. The application accepts file paths as arguments, allowing flexible execution
Automated Reporting
Generates annotated PDFs (audit-<filename>.pdf) with visual indicators for validation
CI/CD Integration
Designed to run seamlessly within GitHub Actions for automated validation on every push. A YAML workflow orchestrates the build and execution by looping through each PDF file and passing it as an argument into the Java application.

🛠️ Technical Design
Language: Java 21
Build Tool: Maven
Automation: GitHub Actions

The application is built around a simple but scalable pattern:
The program accepts a file path as input, processes it, and outputs an audited version.
This allows external systems (like CI pipelines) to control execution without modifying the code.

🔁 How the Automation Works

The GitHub Actions workflow:

Sets up the environment
Builds the project
Loops through all PDF files in /demo-files
Runs the validator for each file

Because of this design:

Adding a new file requires no code changes
The system automatically scales with new inputs

⚙️ How It Scales

The system automatically processes every PDF in the input directory using a CI-driven workflow, requiring no code changes to support new files.

📊 Why This Matters

This approach creates a single source of truth for validation results.
Anyone can view outputs directly from the CI pipeline without running the project locally.
